# Summary From Previous Slides

=== layout: one-panel

# Multiplication Rules

@body

- Specific Multiplication Rule, if two events, A and B, are [independent]{color=red}, then\:
  - [P(A and B) = P(A) × P(B)]{color=red}
- General Multiplication Rule, if two events, A and B, are NOT independent then\:
  - [P(A and B) = P(A) × P(B|A) = P(B) × P(A|B)]{color=blue}

=== layout: one-panel

# Addition Rules

@body

- Specific Addition Rule\: if two events, A and B, are [mutually exclusive]{color=red}, then\:
  - [P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B)]{color=red}
- General Addition Rule\: if two events, A and B, are NOT mutually exclusive, then\:
  - [P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) &ndash; P(A and B)]{color=blue}

