# Question 3.18

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 3](assets/lect05g-more_probability_problems/image_003.png)

=== layout: two-panels


@left

![Slide image 3](assets/lect05g-more_probability_problems/image_003.png)

@right

- only round seeds from F2 generation were selected
- how many F3 wrinkled seeds come from only round seeds...

=== layout: two-panels


@left

![Slide image 3](assets/lect05g-more_probability_problems/image_003.png)

@right

- P: true-breeding RR x rr
- F1: all Rr; round
- F2: 3/4 round; 1/4 wrinkled
- Selected F2 round: 2/3 Rr; 1/3 RR
- Testcross RR x rr: no wrinkled offspring
- Testcross Rr x rr: 1/2 wrinkled offspring
- P(F3 wrinkled) = P(wrinkled | Rr) x P(Rr)
- = 1/2 x 2/3 = 1/3

=== layout: section

# BONUS Question 3.16

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 4](assets/lect05g-more_probability_problems/image_004.png)

=== layout: one-plus-two-panels


@left

- A\: individual tests positive
- B\: individual has disease
- P(A) = P(A and B) + P(A and not B)
- P(A and B)
  - = P(A|B) × P(B) = 1 × 0.002
- P(A and not B)
  - = P(A|not B) × P(not B) = 0.002 × (1&ndash;0.002)
- 1×0.002 + 0.002×(1&ndash;0.002)
  - = [0.003996]{color=red}

@top-right

![Slide image 5](assets/lect05g-more_probability_problems/image_005.png)

@bottom-right

![Slide image 5](assets/lect05g-more_probability_problems/image_004.png)

